 #     An independent host (node\host.json identity.mode) never uses this channel.
 # A release that would drop identity records or release-policy verification is not installed on a host that relies on
 # them, and is not rolled back to.
+# ROLES BESIDE THE RELEASE (ENCLAVE-ROLLBACK-GUARD-V1): on a host where other roles live beside the release (an entry in Program
+# Files\Enclave that no release owns, e.g. host-services\hs2 or challenge-replica, or an \Enclave\ task other than the release's
+# own), a release whose install-host.ps1 lacks ENCLAVE-ROLE-PRESERVATION-V1 is not installed, and a failed install is not rolled
+# back to one: such an installer deletes all of Program Files\Enclave and leaves those roles stopped. The log then says
+# RECOVERY REQUIRED; nothing is reinstalled automatically.
 # Releases older than the running one and the one before it are removed. Log: ProgramData\Enclave\logs\update.log.
